.#-----------------------------------------------------
.input|xwiki/2.1
.# Definition terms without description, at the top level and in a list item: since a term must be followed by a
.# definition description in Markdown, they are followed by an empty definition description, so that they are read
.# back as definition terms (with this additional empty definition description, see list16.test). This isn't done
.# for a term read back as another block (e.g. a standalone macro), which could contain the empty definition
.# description.
.#-----------------------------------------------------
; a
: b
; c
; d

* e
*; f
* g

; {{info}}x{{/info}}

p

; [[https://e.org]]
.#-----------------------------------------------------
.expect|markdown/1.2
.#-----------------------------------------------------
a
:   b

c
d
:   <!-- -->

* e

  f
  :   <!-- -->
* g

{{info}}x{{/info}}

p

<https://e.org>
:   <!-- -->
